From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:05:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Show every player's skin on offline servers

An offline-mode server sends profiles without textures, and the client
asks nobody else, so everyone there is Steve. The Theseus agent now wraps
authlib's texture lookups and, for a player the server sent nothing
usable for, looks the skin up by name: first in a folder of skins put
there by hand, then Ely.by, then Mojang, with capes from OptiFine. A
profile that already carries textures is left alone, so an online-mode
server's signed skins are never second-guessed. Answers are cached, also
across runs, and the game is never kept waiting on the network for long.

The folder is `player_skins` in the launcher directory: `<name>.png` per
player, `<name>-slim.png` for slim arms, with `capes/` and `elytras/`
inside. Settings > Features has the switch, on by default, and a button
that opens the folder. The switch is a feature flag, so it needs no
migration and does not sync to Modrinth.

The agent code comes from Noctrinth (https://github.com/Everelsu/Noctrinth).
